---
// Anatomy of a served answer — illustrative rendering of the format.
---

<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,26rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-12">
  <figure class="answer-card">
    <div class="card-top">
      <span class="mono-label">Question</span>
      <span class="mono-label muted">illustrative</span>
    </div>
    <p class="question">Is a creep test to D<sub>max</sub> = 26 000 v valid for a cell rated E<sub>max</sub> = 30 000 v?</p>

    <div class="verdict">
      <div class="verdict-head">
        <span class="mono-label">Verdict · computed</span>
        <span class="verdict-badge" aria-label="verdict: invalid">INVALID</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="arithmetic" aria-label="Computation"><code>constraint   D_max ≤ 0.8 · E_max
0.8 × 30 000 v = 24 000 v
D_max = 26 000 v
→ exceeds the limit by 2 000 v</code></pre>
      <p class="verdict-src">source: machine model · <span class="cite-chip">R 60-1 model · constraint</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="answer-body">
      <span class="mono-label">Answer</span>
      <p>
        The test is out of scope: for creep testing the maximum test load is bounded at
        <em class="quote">“0.8 · E<sub>max</sub>”</em> — a hard limit of the model, so the verdict is computed rather
        than judged <a class="cite-chip" href="https://ai.oimlsmart.org/">R 60-1:2021 §4.4.2</a>. The cell may be
        tested to D<sub>max</sub> = 24 000 v at most.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="caption">
      Illustrative rendering of the served format. Live answers, with the citations opening the original document at
      the cited clause, are at the reference deployment.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ul class="annotations">
    <li>
      <p class="mono-label">01 · citation</p>
      <p>Every substantive claim names the publication, edition and clause behind it — the reader can go and look.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p class="mono-label">02 · verbatim values</p>
      <p>Normative values are quoted exactly from the source passage, so the claim can be checked mechanically.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p class="mono-label">03 · verdict as data</p>
      <p>The rule is executed, not quoted. The verdict and its arithmetic arrive attached to the answer, and the
        model may not soften or contradict them.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<style>
  .answer-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 0;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(29, 29, 27, 0.04), 0 12px 32px -18px rgba(37, 61, 145, 0.25);
  }
  .card-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .mono-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }
  .muted {
    color: var(--color-rule);
  }
  .question {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .verdict {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(179, 64, 47, 0.35);
    background: rgba(179, 64, 47, 0.05);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
  }
  .verdict-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .verdict-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #fff;
    background: var(--color-signal);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
  }
  .arithmetic {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .verdict-src {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }
  .answer-body {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }
  .answer-body p {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .quote {
    font-style: normal;
    background: #dce6f5;
    padding: 0 0.15em;
  }
  .caption {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }
  .annotations {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1.6rem;
  }
  .annotations li {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .annotations p:last-child {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  .annotations .mono-label {
    color: var(--color-blue);
  }
</style>
